    "summary": "Model built and checked successfully.\n\nBridge: single simply supported span, 30 m between bearing centre-lines, 10 m deck width; 3 precast prestressed small-box girders per span (C40); abutments at both ends on plain laminated elastomeric bearings (300×400 mm, 5×8 mm layers, 2 under each girder end = 6 per line).\n\nRoot cause of the earlier L1/L2 failure (L2-1, no suspect decisions): the instance layer held a stale girder count (n_girders = 4) that contradicted the description's 3 girders per span. The accepted decisions girder.A = 3.417 m², girder.I = 1.065 m⁴, girder.w = 88.84 kN/m and girder.m = 9.056 t/m were all already consistent with n = 3, but the model was assembled from the stale count. Correcting the instance (count_per_span = 3) made MR-02 recompute girder.A/I exactly to the accepted values, and the model passed.\n\nKey results (self-weight + Highway Class II, simply supported):\n- girder.single A = 1.1389 m², I = 0.35492 m⁴ (per girder); combined A = 3.4168 m², I = 1.06475 m⁴\n- Ec = 32500 MPa (C40, JTG 3362-2018 3.1.5), γ = 26.0 kN/m³ (JTG D60-2015 4.2.1)\n- bearing: S = 10.714, Kv = 8.518×10⁶ kN/m, Kh = 18 000 kN/m each line\n- fundamental vertical frequency f1 = 3.402 Hz → impact factor μ = 0.2006\n- lane load: qk = 7.875 kN/m², Pk = 240 kN, reached max positive moment 6449.6 kN·m at midspan\n- self-weight support reactions 1332.5 kN each abutment, midspan moment 9994.1 kN·m"
